  "comments": [
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Bacterial hemolysins are exotoxins that attack blood cell membranes and cause cell rupture. Beta-hemolysin is a phospholipase C with specific activity toward sphingomyelins. Has a high specificity for sphingomyelin, hydrolyzes lysophosphatidylcholine at a much lower rate, but has no activity towards phosphatidylcholine, phosphatidylethanolamine, or phosphatidylserine (By similarity)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
